@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam maxMessageSize 300
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
title Behavior - Confirm delivery mode change
actor "Administrator" as actor
box "Frontend - Mission Control application" #E0F2FE
  participant "ProjectLayoutPage / ProjectHeaderView\nModeChangeDialog / ModeChangeForm" as page
  participant "IWorkspaceService / WorkspaceService" as client
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Api" #D1FADF
  participant "CurrentAccountAuthorization" as access
  participant "WorkspacesController" as ctrl
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Application and Domain" #ECFDF3
  participant "ValidationBehavior" as validation
  participant "ChangeDeliveryModeCommandHandler" as handler
  participant "Workspace" as entity
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Infrastructure" #FFF4E5
  database "Mission Control SQL" as db
end box
actor -> page : Change delivery mode from Project actions on any tab (actionRequested), a paused-sprints banner (overview, Backlog, Board, Sprints; the page relays changeModeRequested), the edit form's link (ProjectFormDialog closes with ChangeMode after the unsaved-changes check), or the work delete dialog's paused-sprint blocker (WorkItemDeleteDialog closes with WorkItemDeleteOutcome ChangeMode; WorkHierarchyPage or WorkItemDetailPage reacts by calling openDialog(ChangeMode)); all shown only with workspaces.changeMode
page -> page : The layout's openDialog(ChangeMode) opens ModeChangeDialog with the workspace the header last resolved; ModeChangeForm receives it as input
alt Loaded workspace has an active sprint
  page --> actor : Blocked state without a request: "Close Sprint N first"; focus Close Sprint N; announce the explanation as an alert; Close only
  opt Close Sprint N
    page -> page : ModeChangeForm emits closeSprintRequested(SprintReference); the dialog closes with CloseSprint(SprintReference); the layout opens CloseSprintDialog with that sprint's ID; on CloseSprintOutcome Closed it calls refresh() and shows the "Sprint 8 closed" toast with its counts through TOAST_SERVICE, and on Outdated it calls refresh(); while that dialog stays open, its unconfirmed output calls refresh() at once, and its forbidden output shows the "Your access changed" toast, without Retry
  end
else No active sprint; Cancel or Escape
  page --> actor : Names the destination mode and what is kept; focus Cancel; Cancel or Escape closes with no request; focus returns to the opener
else No active sprint; Confirm switch
  page -> page : Disable repeat confirmation; show switching progress; draftChange reports pending
  page -> client : changeMode(ChangeDeliveryModeCommand: destination mode, expectedVersion) returns a promise
  client -> access : PUT /api/workspaces/{id}/mode
  access -> access : L2-002 validate signature, issuer, audience, subject, expiry
  access -> db : Read current status, role and credential version
  db --> access : Current account access
  alt Missing, invalid, or expired JWT; inactive account
    access --> client : 401; audit denial without payloads
    client -> client : sessionInterceptor: a 401 for the current session generation calls SessionService.end(Unauthorized) once
    client --> page : The promise rejects with the 401; mode unchanged; navigation to sign-in
  else Collaborator (profile P: no mode changes)
    access --> client : 403; audit denial without payloads
    client -> client : sessionInterceptor calls SessionService.refreshCapabilities() (one in flight)
    client --> page : The promise rejects with the 403; keep the dialog open; explain that only administrators change the delivery mode; switch unavailable, so focus moves to the alert; no reference ID; mode unchanged; controls follow currentSession
  else Administrator
    access -> ctrl : Authorized request
    ctrl -> validation : Send ChangeDeliveryModeCommand through MediatR 12.5.0
    validation -> validation : Mode is Kanban or Scrum; expectedVersion present
    alt Unknown mode or missing version
      validation --> ctrl : 400 field errors; mode unchanged
      ctrl --> client : Validation ProblemDetails
      client --> page : The promise rejects; the dialog's alert shows the field message; no retry or reference ID; the switch becomes unavailable, so focus moves to the alert; mode unchanged
    else Valid request
      validation -> handler : Handle ChangeDeliveryModeCommand
      handler -> db : BeginWorkspaceTransactionAsync(workspaceId): take the workspace lock first (shared with sprint start and allocation)
      alt Lock wait times out
        db --> handler : Lock not acquired; nothing read or changed
        handler --> ctrl : 503 with Retry-After; mode unchanged
        ctrl --> client : ServiceUnavailable ProblemDetails with correlation ID
        client --> page : The promise rejects; keep dialog open in failed state with the reference ID; previous mode kept; no automatic retry; the switch button keeps focus and retries on request
      else Lock acquired; workspace missing
        handler --> ctrl : 404; nothing changed
        ctrl --> client : NotFound ProblemDetails
        client --> page : The promise rejects; ModeChangeForm emits outdated; the dialog closes with Outdated; the layout calls modeChanged(); the header's read fails, so it keeps only the breadcrumb, and the active tab's view shows "Project not found" with Back to projects; focus its heading; no other announcement
      else Lock acquired; version differs from expectedVersion
        handler --> ctrl : L2-041 409 stale version; nothing changed
        ctrl --> client : Conflict ProblemDetails
        client --> page : The promise rejects; ModeChangeForm emits outdated; the dialog closes with Outdated; the layout calls modeChanged(): the header and the active tab reload the current mode and the board route re-matches; once the reloaded header resolves (workspaceLoaded), ProjectLayoutPage shows the info toast "This project changed while the dialog was open. Its current delivery mode is shown." through TOAST_SERVICE, or, when the dialog relayed unconfirmed before this 409, the neutral info toast naming the mode the header now shows ("Community Hackathon 2026 uses Kanban now.")
      else Lock acquired; current version
        handler -> db : Read active sprint under the same lock
        db --> handler : Active sprint or none
        handler -> entity : L2-027 changeMode(destination, activeSprint)
        alt Active sprint exists
          entity --> handler : Rejected: close the sprint first
          handler --> ctrl : 409 naming the active sprint; nothing changed
          ctrl --> client : Conflict ProblemDetails
          client --> page : The promise rejects; switch to the blocked state: "Close Sprint N first" with Close Sprint N; focus it; announce the explanation as an alert; Close only; no retry
        else No active sprint
          entity --> handler : Mode set; IDs, statuses, order, assignments, placements, sprints untouched
          handler -> db : L2-039 / L2-040 AddAuditEvent, then SaveChangesAsync: update Workspace.Mode and version with the success audit; one transaction; lock released
          alt Commit fails unexpectedly
            db --> handler : Roll back mode and audit
            handler --> ctrl : Generic 500 with correlation ID
            ctrl --> client : Failure; mode unchanged
            client --> page : The promise rejects; keep dialog open in the failed state; announce the alert with the reference ID; previous mode kept; the switch button keeps focus and retries only when pressed
          else Commit succeeds
            db --> handler : New committed version
            handler --> ctrl : 204 No Content
            ctrl --> client : Success response
            client --> page : The promise resolves; ModeChangeForm emits changed; the dialog closes with Changed; the layout calls modeChanged(): revision + 1 reloads the header and the active tab, whose tabs and summary follow the new mode; re-navigating the current tab URL lets BoardModeGuard match the board for the new mode; on the sprints route with no Sprints tab in the reloaded header, the layout navigates to overview instead
            page --> actor : The layout shows the "Now using Kanban" or "Now using Scrum" toast through TOAST_SERVICE; focus the project heading
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end
end
opt No response to the switch (timeout or network failure)
  client --> page : The switch may have committed: the dialog stays open; the failed alert reads "We couldn't confirm whether Community Hackathon 2026 switched to Kanban" without a reference ID; ModeChangeForm emits unconfirmed, which the dialog relays
  page -> page : The layout calls modeChanged() at once: revision + 1, so the header and the active tab reread and show the persisted mode; because the dialog is open, the layout defers the re-navigation (BoardModeGuard re-match) and any sprints-to-overview redirect until it closes, since deactivating the active child page, which hosts the dialog, would dismiss it
  page --> actor : The switch resends only when chosen; a switch that did commit makes it meet the stale-version 409, which closes the dialog with Outdated; the deferred re-navigation then runs, and the layout shows the neutral info toast "Community Hackathon 2026 uses Kanban now." naming the mode the reloaded header shows, not the changed-while-open toast; Cancel or Escape closes with no result, and the deferred re-navigation runs then
end
note over ctrl, db
Kanban mode keeps planned/closed sprints readable but paused;
sprint start and allocation return 409 until Scrum returns (L2-027.3).
Unexpected failures return generic 500 plus correlation ID (L2-043).
end note
@enduml
